From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: metaX contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dahlia: verify exact work slug before accepting detail pages

The shared DAHLIA/FALENO scraper previously trusted the requested detail URL.
WordPress can redirect a missing work slug to a different work, which makes
the scraper return unrelated metadata under the requested ID. Query the
WordPress REST API for the exact slug first, then validate the final detail
URL after redirects. Keep the existing HTML field parser unchanged.

Based on metatube-community/metatube-sdk-go commit
c62584675c593816cc07e7b5b977d14c7eb505a3.

---
 provider/dahlia/core/core.go      | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 provider/dahlia/core/core_test.go | 87 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 135 insertions(+)

diff --git a/provider/dahlia/core/core.go b/provider/dahlia/core/core.go
index 59c9eb417151fea4f4bcef38931a1088541d541f..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 100644
--- a/provider/dahlia/core/core.go
+++ b/provider/dahlia/core/core.go
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 package core
 
 import (
+	"encoding/json"
 	"fmt"
 	"net/http"
 	"net/url"
@@ -56,4 +57,8 @@ func (core *Core) GetMovieInfoByURL(rawURL string) (info *model.MovieInfo, err e
 	if err != nil {
 		return
 	}
 
+	if err = core.verifyMovieSlug(id); err != nil {
+		return nil, err
